# Frontend (Vue 3 + TypeScript)

## Vue conventions

- **Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">`.** Options API and
  non-setup composition style are forbidden in new code.
- One component per `.vue` file. File name = component name in
  PascalCase (`UserProfile.vue`).
- Props typed via `defineProps<{...}>()` generics. No runtime prop
  type declarations.
- Emits typed via `defineEmits<{...}>()`. No string-array form.

## TypeScript

- `tsconfig.json` runs in **strict mode**. `any` is a code smell;
  every `any` needs a comment explaining why.
- Prefer `type` aliases over `interface` unless declaration merging is
  actually needed.
- API response types are **generated** from the backend schema (later
  enhancement: `openapi-typescript`). For now, hand-mirror them in
  `src/types/api.ts` and keep in sync.

## State management

- **No state management library** until justified by complexity.
  `ref` + `provide`/`inject` covers most needs in a single-dev app.
- If state grows enough to need Pinia, write an ADR first explaining
  why component-local + provide/inject didn't suffice.
- Server state belongs in `@tanstack/vue-query` (only when fetching
  becomes complex enough to justify it — usually around the 3rd or 4th
  cache-invalidation bug you hit).

## API calls

- Single `fetch` wrapper in `src/api/client.ts` that:
  - Adds `Content-Type: application/json` and credentials
  - Maps non-2xx to typed errors
  - Adds Sentry breadcrumb for every request
- Never `fetch()` directly from components.
- Backend URL comes from `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`. In dev, Vite
  proxy handles same-origin.

## Styling

- Default to scoped `<style>` in components.
- Tailwind is acceptable if added in PLAN — write an ADR if added
  later.
- No CSS-in-JS, no styled-components.

## Routing

- `vue-router` for any app with more than two views.
- Lazy-load route components (`() => import('./X.vue')`).

## Errors and observability

- `@sentry/vue` is initialized in `main.ts` from `VITE_SENTRY_DSN`.
- `app.config.errorHandler` reports to Sentry.
- Never `console.error` and continue — surface errors to the user via
  a toast / inline message.

## Forbidden

- jQuery, lodash (use native ES2024+; `lodash-es` only with ADR)
- `eval`, `new Function`, dangerouslySetInnerHTML equivalents
- Storing tokens in `localStorage` (use HTTP-only cookies via backend)
- Editing `package-lock.json` or `yarn.lock` (we use pnpm)
- React patterns: `useState`, `useEffect`, JSX in `.vue` files
